      "type": "feat",
      "img": "icons/svg/aura.svg",
      "system": {
        "description": "<p>The Clay Dragon primary purpose is to be a flying mount. A creature of your choice can mount the Clay Dragon. When it does, replace the creatures movement with the Clay Dragon. The Clay Dragon moves with the mounted creature. If you are mounted to the Clay Dragon, you cannot command it to move separate from you unless you dismount by spending 5 feet of your normal movement. Attacks targeting the mounted Creature must instead target the Dragon and attacks targeting the Clay Dragon does not harm the mounted creature. Effects that target an area affects only the Clay Dragon.</p>",
